{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A drawing by classical multidimensional scaling of the shortest-path distances: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"coordinates of the best rank-2 approximation of the doubly centred squared distances."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols\/graph\/multidimensionalscalinglayout(edgelength:maxiterations:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/multidimensionalScalingLayout(edgeLength:maxIterations:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"multidimensionalScalingLayout"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"edgeLength"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":" = { _ in 1 }, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maxIterations"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"NoConvergence"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Drawing"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The distance d_ij of two vertices is their shortest-path distance with ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeLength","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (hops by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default); between components it is 1 + L̄·√n, L̄ the mean edge length, as in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"stressMajorizationLayout()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". With B = −½ J D⁽²⁾ J (D⁽²⁾ the squared distances, J the centring","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"matrix), x is √λ₁ · v₁ and y is √λ₂ · v₂ for the two largest eigenvalues λ₁ ≥ λ₂ of B and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their unit eigenvectors (a negative eigenvalue gives 0). When the distances are Euclidean","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in the plane, the drawing reproduces them exactly, up to a rigid motion. Each axis’s sign","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes its first entry, in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, whose magnitude is at least 10⁻⁴ of its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"largest positive. The drawing is centred on the origin. A directed graph is drawn through","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"undirectedView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Torgerson, “Multidimensional scaling: I. Theory and method”, Psychometrika 17(4), 1952."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O(n·(n + m)) for the distances by breadth-first search (O(n·m log n) by Dijkstra when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lengths differ), then O(n³) for the dense eigensystem; n² ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Precondition","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every edge length is positive and finite; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"least 1."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Throws","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"NoConvergence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" after ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" QL iterations in all (30 n when nil), as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"spectralLayout(weight:maxIterations:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"SpectralLayout.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphDrawing\/SpectralLayout.swift#L59"},"modules":[{"name":"GraphDrawing","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"role":"symbol","title":"multidimensionalScalingLayout(edgeLength:maxIterations:)","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P0A7DrawingE29multidimensionalScalingLayout10edgeLength13maxIterationsAD0C0Vy6VertexQzGSd5Edges_5IndexQZXE_SiSgtAA13NoConvergenceVYKF","extendedModule":"GraphPr